1
00:01:08,985 --> 00:01:11,065
[SCREECHING]

2
00:01:17,952 --> 00:01:19,412
[HORN HONKS]

3
00:01:29,422 --> 00:01:30,882
[WHISTLE BLOWS]

4
00:01:34,427 --> 00:01:35,887
[DOG BARKING]

5
00:02:05,834 --> 00:02:07,924
[PEOPLE CLAPPING AND CHEERING]

6
00:02:08,128 --> 00:02:11,668
MAN: Here we are, folks,
on the red carpet at the grand opening...

7
00:02:11,840 --> 00:02:13,970
of the Coolsonian Criminology Museum.

8
00:02:14,134 --> 00:02:17,144
Tonight's premiere exhibit
is a rousing look back...

9
00:02:17,303 --> 00:02:20,013
at the exploits of Mystery lncorporated.

10
00:02:20,390 --> 00:02:22,850
And here they are.

11
00:02:27,730 --> 00:02:30,980
Folks, this crowd is going crazy
over Mystery Inc.

12
00:02:31,151 --> 00:02:33,241
- Fred!
- Fred, we love you!

13
00:02:33,653 --> 00:02:38,703
Here you go, girls.
I got an ascot for each of you.

14
00:02:40,493 --> 00:02:41,833
Hello!

15
00:02:42,245 --> 00:02:47,075
Check it out! It's a Shag and Scoob quake
and the whole city's shaking!

16
00:02:47,250 --> 00:02:48,580
Yeah!

17
00:02:50,253 --> 00:02:51,753
Come on, Scoob.

18
00:02:56,593 --> 00:02:58,263
Oh, sorry.

19
00:02:58,469 --> 00:03:01,179
I consider it a privilege, sir.

20
00:03:01,389 --> 00:03:05,019
GIRLS: Daphne!
- Don't you two look beautiful. Thank you.

21
00:03:05,185 --> 00:03:08,515
Daphne! Daphne! Daphne!

22
00:03:09,022 --> 00:03:14,482
Hi! We love you! We have you tattooed
on our chests! Look!

23
00:03:15,778 --> 00:03:18,028
That's very sweet.

24
00:03:18,865 --> 00:03:20,525
Velma! Velma!

25
00:03:22,869 --> 00:03:24,949
[SCREAMING]

26
00:03:26,497 --> 00:03:30,037
- Sign it, please.
- We love you, Velma.

27
00:03:30,210 --> 00:03:31,460
Thanks.

28
00:03:31,628 --> 00:03:34,798
- I love her so much.
- May I have a word...

29
00:03:35,006 --> 00:03:37,796
- with Coolsville's hottest detectives?
- Absolutely.

30
00:03:38,009 --> 00:03:40,589
That's your word.
Come on, dear. We're late.

31
00:03:40,762 --> 00:03:43,062
Heather Jasper-Howe
at the grand opening...

32
00:03:43,223 --> 00:03:45,643
of the new Coolsonian
Criminology Museum...

33
00:03:45,808 --> 00:03:49,808
with our guests of honor, the master
detectives of Mystery Incorporated.

34
00:03:50,063 --> 00:03:51,733
[SNIFFING]

35
00:03:51,940 --> 00:03:53,320
Shaggy!

36
00:03:53,524 --> 00:03:55,614
Hey!

37
00:03:56,277 --> 00:03:57,567
Right on!

38
00:03:57,737 --> 00:03:59,817
Hello! Hello!

39
00:04:00,031 --> 00:04:02,281
[BARKING]

40
00:04:10,333 --> 00:04:14,673
With all your success, will you still
have time for us in little old Coolsville?

41
00:04:14,837 --> 00:04:18,467
Of course little old Coolsville
can solve its problems without us...

42
00:04:18,633 --> 00:04:20,843
but we'll always be here to help.

43
00:04:21,052 --> 00:04:24,012
The people of Coolsville
are the best in the world!

44
00:04:24,180 --> 00:04:26,310
[CROWD CHEERING]

45
00:04:31,562 --> 00:04:34,192
HEATHER: Fred, can you
tell us a little about the exhibit?

46
00:04:34,357 --> 00:04:36,937
FRED: Absolutely. Mystery Inc.
Is proud to donate...

47
00:04:37,110 --> 00:04:40,570
the costumes of criminals
we've unmasked.

48
00:04:40,863 --> 00:04:44,993
- Like The Black Knight Ghost.
FRED: Our very first case.

49
00:04:45,159 --> 00:04:47,489
- The 10,000 Volt Ghost.
- Uh-huh.

50
00:04:48,705 --> 00:04:53,375
The Skeleton Men,
and even the dreaded Pterodactyl Ghost.

51
00:04:55,378 --> 00:04:59,548
We've also donated the costumes
of some of our more ridiculous foes.

52
00:04:59,716 --> 00:05:01,046
Like Chickenstein.

53
00:05:01,217 --> 00:05:03,797
Can we get a shot of you
next to The Black Night?

54
00:05:03,970 --> 00:05:05,720
Ridiculous? Obviously she forgot...

55
00:05:05,888 --> 00:05:07,808
- that dude tried to pluck us.
- Yeah.

56
00:05:07,974 --> 00:05:10,894
- Remember what I told you?
- Never pick your nose in public?

57
00:05:11,102 --> 00:05:13,562
- No.
- No, but that's good too.

58
00:05:13,730 --> 00:05:16,820
- Image is everything.
- Yes! Image is everything.

59
00:05:16,983 --> 00:05:19,483
The whole city's watching,
so try and keep a brave face.

60
00:05:19,652 --> 00:05:21,112
[GASPS]

61
00:05:21,529 --> 00:05:22,819
They're costumes.

62
00:05:22,989 --> 00:05:24,659
- Oh.
- Oh, right.

63
00:05:24,866 --> 00:05:26,326
[GASPS]

64
00:05:26,659 --> 00:05:31,579
She's right, Scoob.
Up close, they look totally fake.

65
00:05:32,999 --> 00:05:34,419
[YELPS]

66
00:05:34,625 --> 00:05:39,545
The Tar Monster scared the locals
of Byzantius away to take their treasure.

67
00:05:39,839 --> 00:05:42,919
But on the positive side,
he'd pave your driveway for free.

68
00:05:43,134 --> 00:05:44,594
[PEOPLE LAUGHING]

69
00:05:44,761 --> 00:05:46,551
Isn't that right, Velma?

70
00:05:47,764 --> 00:05:49,104
Velma?

71
00:06:04,072 --> 00:06:05,532
[YELLS]
[THUDDING]

72
00:06:15,708 --> 00:06:18,208
- Hi.
- Hi.

73
00:06:18,378 --> 00:06:20,458
Uh... Oh, um...

74
00:06:20,713 --> 00:06:23,263
Daphne, this is Patrick Wisely.

75
00:06:23,424 --> 00:06:27,264
He's the curator here at the museum.

76
00:06:27,428 --> 00:06:29,298
It's very nice to meet you, Patrick.

77
00:06:29,472 --> 00:06:33,812
I hope you'll be working closely with
Velma on this ever-expanding exhibit.

78
00:06:35,478 --> 00:06:38,808
I know that you're a glamorous,
mysterious, jet-set adventurer...

79
00:06:38,981 --> 00:06:41,821
preoccupied with
international intrigue and all...

80
00:06:41,984 --> 00:06:46,114
- Yes. That's me.
- I know, but...

81
00:06:46,989 --> 00:06:51,739
There's a symposium coming up on syntactic
reasoning in the criminal brain...

82
00:06:52,203 --> 00:06:55,163
I have always found
a criminal's inclination...

83
00:06:55,331 --> 00:06:59,961
to incorrectly use the interrogative
pronoun in place of the relative...

84
00:07:00,128 --> 00:07:01,708
delightfully absurd.

85
00:07:02,755 --> 00:07:04,585
- Me too!
- Really?

86
00:07:04,757 --> 00:07:08,087
Yeah. So maybe you'd want
to go together?

87
00:07:09,345 --> 00:07:11,215
Suppose you mean like...

88
00:07:12,140 --> 00:07:13,640
Like a...

89
00:07:14,183 --> 00:07:16,693
Like a date. With me.

90
00:07:16,853 --> 00:07:19,733
Oh, I... No, I can't, Patrick.

91
00:07:19,981 --> 00:07:21,441
Oh.

92
00:07:21,732 --> 00:07:25,242
Mystery is my mistress.
I must heed her sweet call.

93
00:07:25,653 --> 00:07:26,993
Okay.

94
00:07:36,956 --> 00:07:39,036
[THUNDER ROLLS]

95
00:07:44,672 --> 00:07:46,762
[PEOPLE SCREAMING]

96
00:07:50,887 --> 00:07:52,847
VELMA:
What's happening?

97
00:07:53,139 --> 00:07:55,219
[WIND WHISTLING]

98
00:08:04,025 --> 00:08:05,475
[SCREECHING]

99
00:08:06,277 --> 00:08:07,567
Oh, boy.

100
00:08:10,781 --> 00:08:12,161
FRED:
Daphne!

101
00:08:12,325 --> 00:08:14,735
Go, Ned! Get it! Get it!

102
00:08:22,210 --> 00:08:23,670
We need to come up with a plan.

103
00:08:23,836 --> 00:08:26,246
- Hiding is our plan.
- Yeah.

104
00:08:26,422 --> 00:08:30,382
In case you haven't noticed, there's
an unidentified freaky object in here!

105
00:08:32,094 --> 00:08:34,394
- The curtains!
- We're on them!

106
00:08:34,889 --> 00:08:36,929
Come on, you chickens! Grab those ropes!

107
00:08:37,099 --> 00:08:40,309
- Okay.
- But chickens aren't good with ropes!

108
00:08:41,896 --> 00:08:43,516
FRED:
We got him!

109
00:08:43,689 --> 00:08:46,109
VELMA:
Shaggy, use the ropes to tie him up!

110
00:08:46,317 --> 00:08:49,527
SHAGGY: It's just a costume!
It's just a costume!

111
00:08:50,112 --> 00:08:51,322
It's just a costume!

112
00:08:52,198 --> 00:08:53,778
We tied it! Let go!

113
00:08:53,950 --> 00:08:56,030
[LAUGHING]

114
00:09:09,257 --> 00:09:10,917
[SHAGGY YELLING]

115
00:09:12,802 --> 00:09:13,802
Sorry!

116
00:09:13,970 --> 00:09:16,720
- We have to save Shaggy and Scooby!
- As usual!

117
00:09:26,941 --> 00:09:28,651
SCOOBY:
Fire!

118
00:09:30,987 --> 00:09:33,067
Yahoo!

119
00:09:34,490 --> 00:09:38,120
MAN:
Mystery lncorporated.

120
00:09:38,327 --> 00:09:40,407
[LAUGHING EVILLY]

121
00:09:41,497 --> 00:09:45,497
This is only the first rung
on the ladder of your demise.

122
00:09:45,668 --> 00:09:46,788
SHAGGY:
Look out!

123
00:09:54,510 --> 00:09:58,850
And this time,
you'll be the ones unmasked...

124
00:09:59,181 --> 00:10:02,481
as the buffoons you truly are!

125
00:10:07,857 --> 00:10:09,937
[LAUGHING EVILLY]

126
00:10:13,779 --> 00:10:15,819
HEATHER:
Any clues to the cause of the attack?

127
00:10:15,990 --> 00:10:18,030
How did the dinosaur
get through security?

128
00:10:18,200 --> 00:10:20,330
Where did Mystery lnc.'s plan go wrong?

129
00:10:20,786 --> 00:10:22,866
[SPEAKING INDISTINCTLY]

130
00:10:30,379 --> 00:10:32,459
A secret hatch!

131
00:10:33,007 --> 00:10:36,637
The real Pterodactyl Ghost
must have come through here!

132
00:10:43,351 --> 00:10:45,561
A reptilian scale.

133
00:10:46,062 --> 00:10:48,562
A most wonderful clue.

134
00:10:48,731 --> 00:10:53,571
He stole two costumes: The Black Knight
Ghost and The 10,000 Volt Ghost. Why?

135
00:10:53,736 --> 00:10:57,156
Fred, Daphne. Could you answer
a few questions for the press?

136
00:10:58,240 --> 00:11:01,410
Fred, I don't think
that's a really good idea.

137
00:11:01,577 --> 00:11:05,207
We always face the press
after we've unmasked the creeps.

138
00:11:05,373 --> 00:11:07,253
We looked ridiculous back there.

139
00:11:07,458 --> 00:11:11,208
Don't worry about it, sweetheart.
The press loves us.

140
00:11:18,969 --> 00:11:21,759
The higher the pedestal,
the harder the fall.

141
00:11:21,972 --> 00:11:23,262
And Mystery Inc. Fell far...

142
00:11:23,516 --> 00:11:25,926
in the embarrassing debacle...

143
00:11:26,102 --> 00:11:28,942
that tarnished the reputation
of the once-great gang.

144
00:11:29,105 --> 00:11:32,935
It was an utter disaster
as two of the gang's key members...

145
00:11:33,109 --> 00:11:36,109
Norville "shaggy" Rogers
and scoobert "Scooby-Doo"...

146
00:11:36,278 --> 00:11:40,118
caused untold damage to Coolsville's
hottest new tourist attraction...

147
00:11:40,282 --> 00:11:43,032
which took a full two years
to complete.

148
00:11:43,202 --> 00:11:47,622
When asked for comment, Fred Jones,
leader of Mystery lnc., said this:

149
00:11:47,790 --> 00:11:50,460
Coolsville can solve its
problems without us.

150
00:11:50,626 --> 00:11:53,126
I didn't say that! I mean...

151
00:11:53,295 --> 00:11:55,795
I did, but that's out of context!

152
00:11:55,965 --> 00:11:59,625
This is Heather Jasper-Howe,
disillusioned from Coolsville.

153
00:12:03,305 --> 00:12:05,305
It's all my fault.

154
00:12:06,308 --> 00:12:09,308
I'm the one who told Shaggy
and Scooby to get the ropes.

155
00:12:09,812 --> 00:12:11,772
No, Velma, it's my fault.

156
00:12:11,939 --> 00:12:14,319
I should have checked
that they were tied before I let go.

157
00:12:14,483 --> 00:12:16,153
It's my fault too.

158
00:12:16,318 --> 00:12:18,648
We all know how Shaggy
and Scooby can be.

159
00:12:19,071 --> 00:12:20,161
But it's all right.

160
00:12:20,322 --> 00:12:24,082
We just need to stay strong,
in control, and work fast.

161
00:12:24,243 --> 00:12:26,493
Come on, gang. Let's get to the lab.

162
00:12:26,662 --> 00:12:30,002
We'll figure a way out
of this Jurassic jumble.

163
00:12:33,669 --> 00:12:34,999
Shaggy?

164
00:12:36,046 --> 00:12:38,506
- We're screwups.
- Yeah.

165
00:12:38,674 --> 00:12:41,094
I guess, looking back, every time
they made a plan...

166
00:12:41,260 --> 00:12:42,840
we did screw it up somehow.

167
00:12:43,053 --> 00:12:45,263
- I just never noticed before.
- Me neither.

168
00:12:45,431 --> 00:12:49,681
There's gotta be some way we can prove
that we actually belong in the gang.

169
00:12:50,186 --> 00:12:52,646
We've gotta do something
totally unlike us.

170
00:12:52,813 --> 00:12:55,363
- Hmm...
- You know, Scoob...

171
00:12:55,858 --> 00:12:58,528
we could act like real detectives!

172
00:12:59,195 --> 00:13:01,315
[LAUGHING]

173
00:13:01,530 --> 00:13:02,570
Really?

174
00:13:04,700 --> 00:13:09,540
Scooby-Doo, raise your right paw.
No, your right paw. Your other paw.

175
00:13:09,705 --> 00:13:14,535
Repeat after me. From this day forward
we will no longer be our goofy selves.

176
00:13:14,710 --> 00:13:16,380
[SPEAKING GIBBERISH]

177
00:13:16,587 --> 00:13:18,377
We will be awesome detectives.

178
00:13:19,632 --> 00:13:22,972
And we will act more like Fred
and Velma and Daphne.

179
00:13:23,135 --> 00:13:27,385
We will be terrific and fantastic
and spectacular...

180
00:13:27,598 --> 00:13:31,888
and cease to be "loser-iffic,"
"lame-tastic" and "suck-tacular."

181
00:13:32,102 --> 00:13:34,732
Yeah, yeah. Suck-tacular.

182
00:13:36,732 --> 00:13:39,732
Right, like, it's time
to solve the mystery.

183
00:13:39,902 --> 00:13:44,072
- Let's kick this investigation up to an 11!
- Yeah.

184
00:13:44,240 --> 00:13:46,070
What the heck are you guys doing?

185
00:13:46,242 --> 00:13:48,832
We figured the first step
in solving a mystery...

186
00:13:48,994 --> 00:13:51,584
would be to wear the right attire.

187
00:13:51,747 --> 00:13:55,037
I'm sorry, Daph,
but your go-go boots didn't fit...

188
00:13:55,751 --> 00:13:57,341
me!

189
00:13:59,922 --> 00:14:03,592
Scooby! Those so don't go
with that sweater!

190
00:14:03,759 --> 00:14:04,929
Really?

191
00:14:05,553 --> 00:14:07,433
[FAX MACHINE BEEPS]

192
00:14:09,139 --> 00:14:11,929
Ah, clues!

193
00:14:12,142 --> 00:14:15,192
Alas, what are these strange markings?

194
00:14:17,857 --> 00:14:18,937
Words.

195
00:14:19,149 --> 00:14:20,609
Ahh...

196
00:14:20,776 --> 00:14:22,186
Words!

197
00:14:22,653 --> 00:14:24,113
Scooby-Doo, take notes.

198
00:14:24,280 --> 00:14:26,780
- Gotcha.
VELMA: Come on, you kooks.

199
00:14:27,449 --> 00:14:28,699
Okay.

200
00:14:30,369 --> 00:14:32,449
It's come back positive.

201
00:14:32,663 --> 00:14:34,963
This is a real pterodactyl scale.

202
00:14:35,124 --> 00:14:36,124
Precisely!

203
00:14:36,292 --> 00:14:38,632
That masked figure
was out to humiliate us.

204
00:14:39,628 --> 00:14:42,048
Maybe it's someone we unmasked.

205
00:14:42,214 --> 00:14:46,304
But who would be able to make
a real Pterodactyl Ghost?

206
00:14:48,637 --> 00:14:50,807
The original Pterodactyl Ghost.

207
00:14:50,973 --> 00:14:52,473
Dr. Jonathan Jacobo.

208
00:14:52,683 --> 00:14:53,983
VELMA:
That's right!

209
00:14:56,228 --> 00:15:00,318
Jacobo wreaked havoc
in a statewide crime spree.

210
00:15:02,818 --> 00:15:05,318
Jacobo stole millions...

211
00:15:05,487 --> 00:15:09,987
which he used to finance his failed
experiments trying to create monsters.

212
00:15:10,200 --> 00:15:13,080
Come alive! Come alive!

213
00:15:23,839 --> 00:15:26,009
FRED:
You think Jacobo's behind this?

214
00:15:26,342 --> 00:15:30,012
VELMA: Impossible. Three years ago
he attempted a prison escape.

215
00:15:33,349 --> 00:15:35,479
[YELLING]

216
00:15:40,522 --> 00:15:42,862
So long, suckers!

217
00:15:44,234 --> 00:15:45,864
[CREAKING]
[SNAPPING]

218
00:15:46,362 --> 00:15:48,362
Help me, suckers!

219
00:15:49,949 --> 00:15:52,369
His body was lost at sea.

220
00:15:52,534 --> 00:15:57,044
How about this? Jacobo's cellmate was
released from prison two months ago.

221
00:15:57,206 --> 00:15:58,706
Jeremiah Wickles.

222
00:15:58,874 --> 00:16:02,884
The Black Knight Ghost. That was
one of the costumes that was stolen.

223
00:16:03,045 --> 00:16:04,875
Right! And...

224
00:16:05,881 --> 00:16:07,381
Uh...

225
00:16:07,883 --> 00:16:10,303
Scooby-Doo! What's your conclusion?

226
00:16:11,053 --> 00:16:12,393
Bunny.

227
00:16:19,311 --> 00:16:22,561
VELMA: It seems Old Man Wickles
deserves a visit...

228
00:16:23,232 --> 00:16:26,402
before any of our other creepy
conquests make a comeback.

229
00:16:26,568 --> 00:16:28,068
DAPHNE:
Freddy, up on the right.

230
00:16:28,278 --> 00:16:30,908
VELMA:
Old Man Wickles' ancestral manor.

231
00:16:33,826 --> 00:16:36,996
Oh, man. Another creepy crib!

232
00:16:37,413 --> 00:16:41,043
How come we can't ever investigate,
like, a KFC or something?

233
00:16:41,208 --> 00:16:42,248
Shaggy!

234
00:16:43,794 --> 00:16:47,714
All right. Then again,
creepy is my middle name.

235
00:16:47,881 --> 00:16:50,551
Yeah, yeah. Yeah!

236
00:16:52,511 --> 00:16:53,591
Scoob!

237
00:16:57,266 --> 00:16:58,726
Come on, Scoob!

238
00:16:58,892 --> 00:17:01,392
VELMA:
Looks like a bit of a fixer-upper.

239
00:17:02,438 --> 00:17:03,898
Hey!

240
00:17:04,314 --> 00:17:06,324
Nice job last night. Losers!

241
00:17:07,026 --> 00:17:09,436
Quick, we need to think of a comeback.

242
00:17:09,611 --> 00:17:10,951
BOY:
What dorks.

243
00:17:11,113 --> 00:17:13,283
Hey! Shut up!

244
00:17:13,449 --> 00:17:14,909
[LAUGHING]

245
00:17:15,200 --> 00:17:16,830
That's a good one.

246
00:17:17,870 --> 00:17:20,790
MAN OVER LOUDSPEAKER:
You are trespassing on Wickles Manor.

247
00:17:20,956 --> 00:17:24,956
- Leave now or pay the price.
- What jerk makes that his doorbell?

248
00:17:25,419 --> 00:17:28,709
Dude.
He just said we'd pay the price.

249
00:17:28,881 --> 00:17:30,631
Shaggy, Shaggy, Shaggy.

250
00:17:30,799 --> 00:17:34,389
What could possibly happen
by ringing a doorbell?

251
00:17:36,221 --> 00:17:38,311
[SCREAMING]

252
00:17:49,359 --> 00:17:50,739
SCOOBY:
Help me!

253
00:17:51,820 --> 00:17:53,360
Shaggy!

254
00:18:00,662 --> 00:18:02,502
SHAGGY:
I think I pulled something.

255
00:18:02,998 --> 00:18:06,498
That's what can happen
by ringing a doorbell, Fred. That!

256
00:18:06,668 --> 00:18:10,758
MAN OVER LOUDSPEAKER: At 7 p.m.,
the owner will be home to set you free.

257
00:18:10,923 --> 00:18:12,343
GIRL:
Hey.

258
00:18:12,508 --> 00:18:14,508
You want to buy a box of cookies?

259
00:18:15,010 --> 00:18:18,760
Excuse me.
Have you heard the Good News?

260
00:18:18,931 --> 00:18:21,181
Yeah. There's cookies!

261
00:18:21,433 --> 00:18:22,853
Watch the junk!

262
00:18:23,018 --> 00:18:24,188
Sorry.

263
00:18:24,353 --> 00:18:28,863
Oh, brother.
The lock's on a laser thumbprint scanner.

264
00:18:29,024 --> 00:18:31,534
- Let me just get to my makeup.
- Daph, now?

265
00:18:31,693 --> 00:18:35,863
You know what, Velma? It's never too
late to learn to properly apply makeup.

266
00:18:36,031 --> 00:18:39,371
Okay. The last good thumbprint
should still be there, so...

267
00:18:39,535 --> 00:18:41,405
a little blush...

268
00:18:41,912 --> 00:18:43,042
a pore strip...

269
00:18:46,708 --> 00:18:48,208
and voilà.

270
00:18:48,544 --> 00:18:49,884
SHAGGY:
All right, Daph!

271
00:18:50,045 --> 00:18:52,045
I enjoy being a girl.

272
00:18:56,135 --> 00:18:57,385
MAN 1:
Thank you!

273
00:18:57,553 --> 00:18:59,683
MAN 2:
See if I can get my mechanic's job back.

274
00:18:59,847 --> 00:19:01,847
- Twenty, 30, 40...
- Thanks for the cookies.

275
00:19:02,015 --> 00:19:06,225
50... Welcome!
Sixty, 70, 80...

276
00:19:07,437 --> 00:19:11,647
Okay, gang. Let's, like,
split up and search for clues.

277
00:19:11,817 --> 00:19:14,647
Scoob and I will go this way.
Come on, Scoob.

278
00:19:15,154 --> 00:19:17,664
He stole my thing that I say!

279
00:19:30,085 --> 00:19:33,455
Search for clues. Search for clues.

280
00:19:34,423 --> 00:19:35,883
Huh?

281
00:19:36,300 --> 00:19:39,760
Aha! A clue!

282
00:19:46,852 --> 00:19:48,942
Shiny footprints.

283
00:19:49,479 --> 00:19:53,269
VELMA: The glow is similar
to the pterodactyl scale.

284
00:19:58,447 --> 00:19:59,947
Aha!

285
00:20:03,952 --> 00:20:05,372
A clue!

286
00:20:06,288 --> 00:20:08,078
VELMA:
It looks like Wickles shares...

287
00:20:08,248 --> 00:20:11,208
Jacobo's fascination
with the supernatural.

288
00:20:11,627 --> 00:20:15,547
He collects everything
from Piri Reis to Aleister Crowley.

289
00:20:15,797 --> 00:20:17,877
He collects dust too.

290
00:20:18,050 --> 00:20:21,720
No. The dust is good.
We can tell what he's been reading lately.

291
00:20:23,388 --> 00:20:24,638
Like here!

292
00:20:25,057 --> 00:20:26,387
What is it?

293
00:20:26,892 --> 00:20:31,902
It's an obsolete Celtic text used by
secret societies in the mid-19th century.

294
00:20:33,523 --> 00:20:36,323
DAPHNE:
Look. The book belonged to J. Jacobo.

295
00:20:36,985 --> 00:20:38,815
The original Pterodactyl Ghost.

296
00:20:39,029 --> 00:20:41,819
Maybe he gave it to Wickles
before he died.

297
00:20:53,293 --> 00:20:55,803
[PHONOGRAPH PLAYS
SIR MIX-A-LOT'S "BABY GOT BACK"]

298
00:20:56,004 --> 00:20:58,094
[COUGHING]

299
00:21:01,343 --> 00:21:02,763
DAPHNE:
Can you read it?

300
00:21:04,846 --> 00:21:08,426
It's an amalgamation
of magic and science.

301
00:21:08,600 --> 00:21:10,180
Here's a list of ingredients...

302
00:21:10,352 --> 00:21:12,692
on how to create
your own carbon-based...

303
00:21:12,854 --> 00:21:14,944
organic, composite predators.

304
00:21:15,107 --> 00:21:17,357
This is an instruction manual
on how to create...

305
00:21:17,567 --> 00:21:19,357
- monsters.
- Monsters.

306
00:21:24,199 --> 00:21:25,369
Scoob.

307
00:21:25,701 --> 00:21:27,201
Clues!

308
00:21:29,204 --> 00:21:32,714
Those aren't clues, Scoob.
Those are just things you want.

309
00:21:32,874 --> 00:21:35,584
Like, why is a toilet brush a clue?

310
00:21:36,211 --> 00:21:38,551
[SINGING TO THE TUNE
OF "STRANGERS IN THE NIGHT"]

311
00:21:39,381 --> 00:21:44,221
Just because you can sing in it doesn't
make it a clue. It makes it awesome.

312
00:21:45,637 --> 00:21:47,717
[SINGING]

313
00:21:51,518 --> 00:21:55,188
Hey... Like, what's this?

314
00:21:56,481 --> 00:21:58,401
"The Faux Ghost."

315
00:21:58,567 --> 00:22:02,147
We're in luck.
It's tonight, Scoob!

316
00:22:02,988 --> 00:22:04,908
- We are detectives.
- Really?

317
00:22:05,115 --> 00:22:07,615
You found an actual clue!

318
00:22:09,745 --> 00:22:11,405
I found a clue!

319
00:22:12,914 --> 00:22:15,084
Do the clue dance! Do the clue dance!

320
00:22:15,250 --> 00:22:17,590
We're going back, we're going back!

321
00:22:18,170 --> 00:22:20,250
[MAN LAUGHING EVILLY]

322
00:22:28,847 --> 00:22:30,767
Black Knight Ghost!

323
00:22:37,439 --> 00:22:39,019
Run, Shaggy!

324
00:22:40,192 --> 00:22:41,282
Let's go.

325
00:22:42,027 --> 00:22:44,027
SHAGGY:
Like, lock the door!

326
00:22:48,867 --> 00:22:50,277
Heavy stuff, Scoob!

327
00:22:52,954 --> 00:22:54,624
Give me a hand, Scoob!

328
00:22:54,790 --> 00:22:57,170
See him get through this!

329
00:22:57,459 --> 00:22:58,789
SCOOBY:
Heavy!

330
00:23:00,045 --> 00:23:02,295
SHAGGY:
We outsmarted that moron!

331
00:23:02,464 --> 00:23:04,804
Yeah! What a moron.

332
00:23:05,801 --> 00:23:07,221
Look at me.

333
00:23:07,677 --> 00:23:10,297
- Thanks.
BLACK KNIGHT: You're welcome.

334
00:23:19,147 --> 00:23:20,977
- Yo, metalhead!
- Yes?

335
00:23:21,566 --> 00:23:22,816
Bring it.

336
00:23:27,322 --> 00:23:28,992
He brought it.

337
00:23:35,205 --> 00:23:36,825
Daphne! Hold him off!

338
00:23:36,998 --> 00:23:38,498
I'll look in the book.

339
00:23:38,708 --> 00:23:41,668
Maybe there's a formula
for finding his weakness.

340
00:23:47,300 --> 00:23:50,090
Here. "To find a creature's
weakest point..."

341
00:23:51,513 --> 00:23:55,023
take the angle between
the current position of the sun...

342
00:23:56,017 --> 00:23:58,517
- "...and your geographical point..."
- Velma!

343
00:23:59,187 --> 00:24:02,437
VELMA: "Add this point, 28 and a half
feet up from sea level."

344
00:24:04,609 --> 00:24:06,029
That tickles.

345
00:24:06,236 --> 00:24:07,696
This is bad.

346
00:24:07,863 --> 00:24:09,863
VELMA:
"Multiply this number..."

347
00:24:11,241 --> 00:24:12,951
"Add the square inches of..."

348
00:24:16,371 --> 00:24:17,541
Velma!

349
00:24:23,545 --> 00:24:25,165
VELMA:
"Take the square root..."

350
00:24:32,137 --> 00:24:34,467
BLACK KNIGHT:
Now it's good night, ladies!

351
00:24:35,807 --> 00:24:37,017
VELMA:
"your X-axis."

352
00:24:39,561 --> 00:24:41,021
Oh.

353
00:24:58,079 --> 00:25:01,749
VELMA:
"And subtract 9034. That's your Y-axis."

354
00:25:01,917 --> 00:25:03,917
Look. No hands!

355
00:25:04,085 --> 00:25:05,915
Any time would be great, Velma!

356
00:25:06,087 --> 00:25:07,167
VELMA:
I'm trying.

357
00:25:07,339 --> 00:25:11,589
"Subtract one, divide by B,
follow upward eight degrees north."

358
00:25:11,760 --> 00:25:13,930
Which makes his weakest point right here!

359
00:25:18,099 --> 00:25:20,519
Right in the roundtables.

360
00:25:20,685 --> 00:25:21,765
Run!

361
00:25:21,937 --> 00:25:24,267
SCOOBY:
In your face! Scooby-Dooby-Doo!

362
00:25:24,439 --> 00:25:26,609
SHAGGY:
Come on, Scoob! Inside!

363
00:25:30,278 --> 00:25:33,778
VELMA: I'll compare the glow of those
footprints to the pterodactyl scale.

364
00:25:33,949 --> 00:25:35,949
FRED:
We'll check out Wickles' book.

365
00:25:36,117 --> 00:25:38,447
Dude, The Faux Ghost
is an awesome clue.

366
00:25:38,620 --> 00:25:40,120
- Yeah.
- But what do we do with it?

367
00:25:40,288 --> 00:25:42,118
Let's solve the mystery.

368
00:25:42,457 --> 00:25:44,577
If we solve the mystery by ourselves...

369
00:25:44,751 --> 00:25:47,631
it would certainly prove to the gang
that we belong.

370
00:25:47,796 --> 00:25:49,756
- Yeah.
- Let's head to The Faux Ghost...

371
00:25:49,923 --> 00:25:52,053
find Wickles, and see what he knows.

372
00:25:52,217 --> 00:25:56,137
But first, let's give the gang
the old "slipperooney."

373
00:26:05,272 --> 00:26:06,982
Hey, guys.

374
00:26:07,148 --> 00:26:09,478
Scooby's feeling kind of...

375
00:26:10,151 --> 00:26:11,571
like he's got rabies.

376
00:26:11,736 --> 00:26:13,816
[MOANING]

377
00:26:16,658 --> 00:26:20,368
We're just gonna go outside
to get some fresh air.

378
00:26:22,789 --> 00:26:24,249
[MOANING]

379
00:26:32,507 --> 00:26:33,877
Jinkies!

380
00:26:40,015 --> 00:26:41,675
What's up, Velms?

381
00:26:41,891 --> 00:26:44,271
VELMA:
The analysis of the pterodactyl scale.

382
00:26:44,436 --> 00:26:47,346
It contains randamonium,
which this books says...

383
00:26:47,522 --> 00:26:50,322
is the critical ingredient
needed to make monsters.

384
00:26:50,483 --> 00:26:54,033
Doesn't randamonium glow,
like those footprints in Wickles' mansion?

385
00:26:54,195 --> 00:26:58,025
If we prove Wickles is behind this,
this mystery goes down like a dot-com...

386
00:26:58,199 --> 00:27:01,199
- and Coolsville digs us again.
- Where would he get randamonium?

387
00:27:01,369 --> 00:27:04,539
Randamonium is the byproduct
of silver mines.

388
00:27:04,706 --> 00:27:07,706
Like the abandoned mining town
in old Coolsville.

389
00:27:07,917 --> 00:27:10,707
Then we better get to that mining town
and see what's...

390
00:27:13,048 --> 00:27:15,338
I'm invisible. I'm invisible.

391
00:27:17,886 --> 00:27:19,046
Get rid of him!

392
00:27:19,929 --> 00:27:21,679
Keep him busy.

393
00:27:26,061 --> 00:27:27,731
What are you doing?

394
00:27:28,063 --> 00:27:30,063
He wants to ask me on a date.

395
00:27:30,231 --> 00:27:31,901
DAPHNE:
It's okay to be scared.

396
00:27:32,067 --> 00:27:35,737
I am not scared.
I've fought werewolves and ghosts.

397
00:27:35,945 --> 00:27:40,405
But in the end, we usually unmask them
and it's a little scared man inside.

398
00:27:40,575 --> 00:27:42,525
It's the same with dating.

399
00:27:43,578 --> 00:27:47,578
Velma, have you ever considered
that maybe werewolves and ghosts...

400
00:27:47,749 --> 00:27:51,589
are just distractions to keep you away
from what really frightens you?

401
00:27:51,753 --> 00:27:53,593
Intimacy with another person.

402
00:27:53,755 --> 00:27:57,045
And by intimacy, I mean someone
who thinks you're really hot.

403
00:27:58,718 --> 00:28:02,928
But I'm more comfortable
in the world of logic and facts.

404
00:28:04,099 --> 00:28:06,059
And...

405
00:28:07,102 --> 00:28:10,902
I'm not hot.

406
00:28:13,483 --> 00:28:15,113
Me neither.

407
00:28:15,276 --> 00:28:19,066
Everybody has flaws, Velma.
The object of a healthy relationship...

408
00:28:19,239 --> 00:28:22,239
is to never let the other person
know they're there.

409
00:28:22,951 --> 00:28:24,791
- To museums.
- To museums.

410
00:28:25,370 --> 00:28:28,210
Daph, I really like this guy.

411
00:28:28,373 --> 00:28:30,463
What would you do if someone thought...

412
00:28:30,625 --> 00:28:36,085
that you were some glamorous
and mysterious jet-setter?

413
00:28:39,134 --> 00:28:40,764
I'd make myself one.

414
00:28:53,273 --> 00:28:55,273
Who's your mommy?

415
00:28:57,736 --> 00:28:59,316
My... My mommy?

416
00:28:59,529 --> 00:29:02,029
VELMA:
Come on, let's solve a mystery.

417
00:29:06,786 --> 00:29:08,246
Ow.

418
00:29:18,047 --> 00:29:19,507
PATRICK:
Uh, Velma?

419
00:29:19,674 --> 00:29:23,844
- Do you have to go to the bathroom?
- No, I can't in this outfit.

420
00:29:41,321 --> 00:29:43,361
[MEN SPEAKING INDISTINCTLY]

421
00:29:43,615 --> 00:29:46,325
SHAGGY:
Okay, Scooby-Doo, the coast is clear.

422
00:29:46,493 --> 00:29:48,373
SCOOBY:
Here we go.

423
00:29:56,377 --> 00:29:59,377
SHAGGY:
That's it, Scoob. The Faux Ghost.

424
00:29:59,589 --> 00:30:01,629
Man, I recognize a lot of these cats.

425
00:30:01,800 --> 00:30:05,300
Like, that's C.L. Magnus.
He used to dress up as Redbeard's ghost.

426
00:30:05,470 --> 00:30:09,140
And that's Aggie Wilkins,
a.k.a. the Ozark Witch.

427
00:30:09,724 --> 00:30:11,734
These are all folks we unmasked.

428
00:30:11,893 --> 00:30:14,903
If they spot us,
they'll invite us to a weenie roast.

429
00:30:15,104 --> 00:30:17,404
One where we're the weenies!

430
00:30:17,607 --> 00:30:19,727
Mmm, hot dogs!

431
00:30:19,901 --> 00:30:23,991
There's gotta be some way that we can
use our awesome, fearless new skills...

432
00:30:24,155 --> 00:30:27,405
to get us in there
without being recognized.

433
00:30:27,617 --> 00:30:29,697
[SINGING "NU FLOW"]

434
00:30:55,061 --> 00:30:57,271
Hey, hey, hey!

435
00:30:57,438 --> 00:30:59,858
Everyone part like the Red Sea.

436
00:31:00,024 --> 00:31:04,284
It's me, Shizzy McCreepy,
and my brother, S.D. McCrawley.

437
00:31:04,445 --> 00:31:08,275
- Oh, yeah.
- We are in the house and ready to party.

438
00:31:09,242 --> 00:31:10,452
Hey, handsome.

439
00:31:10,618 --> 00:31:12,448
Hello, baby.

440
00:31:15,081 --> 00:31:16,581
- Zoinks!
- Jinkies!

441
00:31:16,749 --> 00:31:18,289
- Hey, gang.
- Jinkies!

442
00:31:18,459 --> 00:31:19,749
- Hey!
- Yipe!

443
00:31:23,590 --> 00:31:28,140
A Ghost Clown is a heck of a lot scarier
than a Cotton Candy Glob!

444
00:31:28,303 --> 00:31:29,973
[YELLING]

445
00:31:31,472 --> 00:31:33,562
Watch out, idiot.

446
00:31:35,560 --> 00:31:38,560
- Old Man Wickles!
- Leave me alone.

447
00:31:40,315 --> 00:31:41,315
No!

448
00:31:41,482 --> 00:31:46,322
I just... I just wanted to say thank you.

449
00:31:46,779 --> 00:31:52,079
Your portrayal of the Black Knight Ghost
was inspirational to my brother and me.

450
00:31:52,285 --> 00:31:53,575
Hey...

451
00:31:53,745 --> 00:31:57,825
Have you done anything cool
and creepy lately?

452
00:31:58,708 --> 00:32:02,338
Listen, I'm not normally one
for giving advice...

453
00:32:02,503 --> 00:32:07,013
but I feel sorry for you because
of your brother's hideous nose deformity.

454
00:32:09,969 --> 00:32:12,719
Get out of this game
while you got a chance.

455
00:32:13,848 --> 00:32:16,178
All of us here ain't nothing to admire.

456
00:32:16,351 --> 00:32:19,351
We needed people to believe
we were different than we were.

457
00:32:19,520 --> 00:32:21,360
Maybe because we believed...

458
00:32:21,522 --> 00:32:25,232
that there was something wrong
with who we were in the first place.

459
00:32:26,194 --> 00:32:30,954
I guess you're sort of grateful
to Mystery lnc...

460
00:32:31,866 --> 00:32:35,036
- for unmasking you.
- Are you kidding?

461
00:32:36,871 --> 00:32:40,711
If I see those twerps,
I'd tear their eyes out of their skulls.

462
00:32:41,542 --> 00:32:42,832
Make them eat the one eye...

463
00:32:43,002 --> 00:32:46,002
while watching themselves
eat it with the other eye!

464
00:32:49,175 --> 00:32:50,215
Bye.

465
00:32:51,844 --> 00:32:53,224
Here's a clue for you.

466
00:32:53,388 --> 00:32:57,178
- That dude's wearing his freak hat 24/7.
- Yeah.

467
00:32:57,350 --> 00:33:00,730
I gotta take a whiz.
Don't do anything to attract attention.

468
00:33:00,895 --> 00:33:02,185
Gotcha.

469
00:33:02,522 --> 00:33:03,862
Hey, doll.

470
00:33:04,649 --> 00:33:06,399
You wanna dance?

471
00:33:06,567 --> 00:33:07,777
Groovy.

472
00:33:10,530 --> 00:33:12,280
Here we go.

473
00:33:12,991 --> 00:33:15,701
[BAND SINGING "THANK YOU
(FALLETIN ME BE MICE ELF AGAIN)"]

474
00:33:16,327 --> 00:33:18,197
WOMAN:
Shake it, baby.

475
00:33:23,710 --> 00:33:25,790
[BARKING]

476
00:33:26,254 --> 00:33:27,844
SCOOBY:
Give me five!

477
00:33:51,863 --> 00:33:53,283
Oh, yeah!

478
00:33:54,615 --> 00:33:56,115
Everybody!

479
00:34:03,458 --> 00:34:05,538
Yahoo!

480
00:34:12,258 --> 00:34:13,798
Oh, yeah.

481
00:34:14,719 --> 00:34:15,759
Hey, Shaggy!

482
00:34:31,152 --> 00:34:33,282
[SCOOBY SINGING]

483
00:34:34,614 --> 00:34:36,074
Hey!

484
00:34:36,324 --> 00:34:39,834
It's Scooby-Doo! The meddling mutt
what helped throw us in jail!

485
00:34:40,953 --> 00:34:43,413
SCOOBY:
Who, me? Uh-uh.

486
00:34:44,957 --> 00:34:47,627
No, wait, that's not Scooby-Doo!

487
00:34:47,794 --> 00:34:51,384
That's S.D. McCrawley.
He's just wearing a mask.

488
00:34:57,178 --> 00:35:02,098
And that's Doo's beatnik best pal,
Shaggy Rogers.

489
00:35:02,266 --> 00:35:04,386
- Where?
- There.

490
00:35:05,019 --> 00:35:07,309
Zoinks! Gangway!

491
00:35:10,108 --> 00:35:12,528
Run, Shaggy. Wait for me!

492
00:35:12,693 --> 00:35:14,823
[YELLING]

493
00:35:18,533 --> 00:35:20,333
MAN:
And stay out!

494
00:35:24,664 --> 00:35:27,674
That wasn't so bad, Scoob.

495
00:35:42,723 --> 00:35:44,353
[SQUEAKING]

496
00:35:44,559 --> 00:35:47,019
That was my outfit, I swear.

497
00:35:51,482 --> 00:35:52,942
