- We're gonna die quickly!

742
00:53:12,772 --> 00:53:14,692
GHOST:
Wait for me!

743
00:53:26,119 --> 00:53:28,249
[SCREAMING]

744
00:53:31,917 --> 00:53:33,037
Come on, girls!

745
00:53:35,795 --> 00:53:38,795
SHAGGY: An exit!
SCOOBY: Run, Shaggy!

746
00:53:50,227 --> 00:53:52,017
MAN:
Stop them!

747
00:53:52,646 --> 00:53:57,896
Destroy the city if you have to,
but get me that control panel!

748
00:53:58,068 --> 00:54:02,818
With it, they can destroy everything
I've set out to do.

749
00:54:02,989 --> 00:54:05,659
FRED: Hurry up, gang.
We need to find Shaggy and Scooby.

750
00:54:05,825 --> 00:54:08,735
GHOST:
End of the line, Mystery Inc.!

751
00:54:10,830 --> 00:54:11,830
Die!

752
00:54:18,171 --> 00:54:20,011
SHAGGY:
Let's book, Scoob.

753
00:54:25,595 --> 00:54:26,845
SCOOBY:
Oh, boy.

754
00:54:29,015 --> 00:54:30,425
Let's rip it, Scoob!

755
00:54:31,017 --> 00:54:32,347
Zoinks!

756
00:54:46,700 --> 00:54:48,370
[YELLING]

757
00:54:48,576 --> 00:54:49,866
SKELETON 1:
I don't know.

758
00:54:52,789 --> 00:54:55,039
SKELETON 2: Banzai!
SKELETON 1: Woo-hoo!

759
00:54:55,208 --> 00:54:56,878
SHAGGY:
We're getting rad!

760
00:54:57,544 --> 00:55:00,594
Like, this pipe's ripping, Scoob!
Zoinks!

761
00:55:31,619 --> 00:55:32,659
Hello.

762
00:55:45,133 --> 00:55:46,343
Scooby!

763
00:55:56,519 --> 00:55:57,639
Are you guys okay?

764
00:55:58,146 --> 00:56:02,936
Sure. As long as you define "okay"
as "in massive agony."

765
00:56:03,109 --> 00:56:04,399
Yeah.

766
00:56:04,611 --> 00:56:06,451
We should get back to headquarters.

767
00:56:06,654 --> 00:56:09,284
No! That'll be the first place
they'll look for us.

768
00:56:09,449 --> 00:56:11,029
I think I know where to go.

769
00:56:12,952 --> 00:56:15,622
Move that worthless piece of tin!

770
00:56:15,955 --> 00:56:19,665
Unlike some of you,
I have a very important meeting!

771
00:56:24,255 --> 00:56:26,295
[YELLING AND SCREAMING]

772
00:56:31,471 --> 00:56:35,221
Citizens! Turn in Mystery lnc.

773
00:56:35,392 --> 00:56:40,062
Your reward: We'll let you live.

774
00:56:40,271 --> 00:56:41,731
[LAUGHING EVILLY]

775
00:56:42,732 --> 00:56:47,402
My monsters can make life
very unpleasant.

776
00:56:47,987 --> 00:56:49,907
[ROARING]

777
00:56:57,997 --> 00:57:02,837
EVIL MASKED FIGURE:
Find me Mystery lnc., now.

778
00:57:03,336 --> 00:57:07,506
Heather Jasper-Howe with an emergency
update for lnvestigative Probe.

779
00:57:07,715 --> 00:57:10,335
A monster army has invaded Coolsville.

780
00:57:10,510 --> 00:57:14,350
Angry citizens have gathered
outside Mystery lnc.'s offices in protest.

781
00:57:14,514 --> 00:57:18,524
They're insisting the gang cooperate
with the Evil Masked Figure's demands.

782
00:57:18,685 --> 00:57:20,845
Mystery Stink! Mystery Stink!

783
00:57:24,858 --> 00:57:28,028
Excuse me, sir.
Do you have anything to say for yourself?

784
00:57:31,823 --> 00:57:33,873
[LAUGHING]

785
00:57:36,536 --> 00:57:38,446
I beg you, Mystery lnc.

786
00:57:38,621 --> 00:57:42,041
If you can hear me, turn yourselves in.

787
00:57:42,250 --> 00:57:46,710
If we do, he'll get the control panel back,
and the city will be in worse shape.

788
00:57:46,880 --> 00:57:49,720
We'd be playing right into his hands.

789
00:57:49,883 --> 00:57:52,973
Please. For our city's sake.

790
00:57:53,470 --> 00:57:55,550
[POUNDING]

791
00:57:59,893 --> 00:58:02,903
Sorry. You're cancelled.

792
00:58:30,340 --> 00:58:33,260
The old high-school clubhouse.

793
00:58:35,428 --> 00:58:37,758
We should be safe here.

794
00:58:37,931 --> 00:58:40,561
We haven't been here in years.

795
00:58:49,817 --> 00:58:51,437
Freddy, are you okay?

796
00:58:52,278 --> 00:58:55,738
- Do you wanna talk?
- Talking's for wimps.

797
00:59:00,954 --> 00:59:02,704
It's time for action.

798
00:59:05,416 --> 00:59:06,786
You know, Scoob...

799
00:59:06,960 --> 00:59:11,550
this Evil Masked Figure
is turning Coolsville into Ghoulsville.

800
00:59:11,798 --> 00:59:14,048
And the gang is totally
taking a hit for it.

801
00:59:14,217 --> 00:59:15,627
Yeah.

802
00:59:16,594 --> 00:59:20,104
Like, this is the most "our-faultiest"
screwup ever, Scoob.

803
00:59:20,265 --> 00:59:22,345
[WHIMPERING]

804
00:59:24,978 --> 00:59:26,598
Still works.

805
00:59:28,064 --> 00:59:30,944
Look, all my old tools.

806
00:59:33,111 --> 00:59:36,151
After all our so-called success...

807
00:59:36,322 --> 00:59:38,492
we're back in this old firetrap.

808
00:59:54,090 --> 00:59:55,590
SHAGGY:
Hit me, Fred.

809
00:59:57,176 --> 00:59:59,176
VELMA:
Oh, Shaggy.

810
01:00:04,183 --> 01:00:06,773
SHAGGY:
Good throw, Velm!

811
01:00:07,395 --> 01:00:10,305
FRED: Gotcha!
- Hey!

812
01:00:11,983 --> 01:00:14,443
Shaggy, throw it to me!

813
01:00:14,611 --> 01:00:16,191
- Go long!
- Okay.

814
01:00:17,030 --> 01:00:19,320
DAPHNE: Go, Scooby!
SHAGGY: Go, Scooby-Doo!

815
01:00:20,158 --> 01:00:21,658
Dude!

816
01:00:26,914 --> 01:00:29,424
It all seemed so easy back then.

817
01:00:30,335 --> 01:00:31,785
Yeah.

818
01:00:32,211 --> 01:00:37,011
We solved mysteries for the love of them,
not to prove anything to anyone.

819
01:00:37,216 --> 01:00:42,886
Yeah. And the mysteries all seemed
to unravel themselves.

820
01:00:43,056 --> 01:00:46,886
Sometimes, the answers
would just appear like magic.

821
01:00:47,143 --> 01:00:48,813
Hey.

822
01:00:49,020 --> 01:00:51,900
My first multiple-resonance
imaging device.

823
01:00:52,065 --> 01:00:56,025
Made out of a crystal radio
and old video games.

824
01:00:57,904 --> 01:00:59,454
Wait a minute.

825
01:00:59,947 --> 01:01:04,737
Randamonium has an algorithmic
cross-currency of negative 4.121.

826
01:01:05,244 --> 01:01:07,414
With it, maybe...
Well, just maybe...

827
01:01:07,580 --> 01:01:11,080
We could reverse the current
and reverse the monster-making process!

828
01:01:11,250 --> 01:01:13,920
Yes. All we need to do
is rewire the control panel...

829
01:01:14,087 --> 01:01:16,757
Bring it back to the Monster Hive
and plug it into the base.

830
01:01:16,923 --> 01:01:20,513
- Right. Push the button...
- And instead of creating monsters...

831
01:01:20,677 --> 01:01:22,757
all the monsters will be destroyed.

832
01:01:55,086 --> 01:01:57,956
Like, they're totally having
a montage in there without us.

833
01:01:58,131 --> 01:01:59,631
Yeah.

834
01:02:00,299 --> 01:02:04,969
I'll tell you one thing for sure.
They don't need our help to figure it out.

835
01:02:05,138 --> 01:02:06,808
- We're screwups.
- Yeah.

836
01:02:07,014 --> 01:02:08,814
The only time we do anything right...

837
01:02:08,975 --> 01:02:11,725
is when we accidentally plow
into the Snow Ghost...

838
01:02:11,894 --> 01:02:16,114
because we've accidentally glued our
feet to rocket-powered roller-skates.

839
01:02:16,274 --> 01:02:19,154
Yeah. Eight stupid times.

840
01:02:20,653 --> 01:02:22,153
SHAGGY:
Face it, Scoob.

841
01:02:22,321 --> 01:02:25,661
We'll never be anything
but our old goofy selves.

842
01:02:26,534 --> 01:02:28,494
I wish once...

843
01:02:28,661 --> 01:02:30,501
just once...

844
01:02:30,830 --> 01:02:33,540
I could do the right thing on purpose.

845
01:02:35,168 --> 01:02:38,168
- You know, Scoob?
- Yeah.

846
01:02:38,546 --> 01:02:40,336
Like, be a hero...

847
01:02:41,174 --> 01:02:43,054
and save the day.

848
01:02:45,553 --> 01:02:47,553
But who are we kidding, right?

849
01:02:59,692 --> 01:03:01,322
Captain Cutler's Ghost.

850
01:03:02,570 --> 01:03:06,320
Captain Cutler's Ghost!

851
01:03:07,700 --> 01:03:11,830
They found us. Finish that in the van
when we get to the Monster Hive.

852
01:03:12,580 --> 01:03:16,210
VELMA: Come on, guys! In the van!
SHAGGY: Hurry!

853
01:03:16,459 --> 01:03:18,539
[ROARING]

854
01:03:19,962 --> 01:03:22,212
SHAGGY:
Go, Fred! Hit it!

855
01:03:25,885 --> 01:03:27,385
Yikes!

856
01:03:33,100 --> 01:03:34,680
- What do we do?
- What do we do?

857
01:03:34,852 --> 01:03:36,602
FRED:
Fine. Let's go back!

858
01:03:38,064 --> 01:03:39,864
SHAGGY:
That's the wrong way!

859
01:03:53,079 --> 01:03:54,749
Shaggy! Give me a hand.

860
01:03:54,914 --> 01:03:57,584
This is tied for
the most terrifying day of my life.

861
01:03:57,750 --> 01:04:01,040
- Tied with what?
- Every other freaking day of my life!

862
01:04:01,212 --> 01:04:02,252
It's done!

863
01:04:08,427 --> 01:04:10,547
[SCREECHING]

864
01:04:12,139 --> 01:04:14,099
Jinkies! Tweety's back.

865
01:04:14,267 --> 01:04:15,517
- Shaggy!
- Yeah?

866
01:04:15,685 --> 01:04:18,395
I'm putting her in cruise.
Take the wheel.

867
01:04:18,563 --> 01:04:20,153
Go!

868
01:04:31,242 --> 01:04:32,282
Take this!

869
01:04:35,454 --> 01:04:38,254
- This is bad.
- No doubt.

870
01:04:39,458 --> 01:04:40,628
- Shaggy?
- Yeah.

871
01:04:40,793 --> 01:04:42,293
- Who's driving?
- Uh...

872
01:04:43,921 --> 01:04:44,961
Hello.

873
01:04:45,131 --> 01:04:46,421
SHAGGY: Scoob.
- What?

874
01:04:49,218 --> 01:04:51,298
[SCREAMING]

875
01:05:01,439 --> 01:05:04,399
- Scooby, turn the wheel!
- Wheel?

876
01:05:04,567 --> 01:05:07,487
FRED: Scooby, turn the wheel!
SHAGGY: The round thing, Scoob!

877
01:05:14,118 --> 01:05:16,488
- Scooby!
- Okay.

878
01:05:23,002 --> 01:05:24,672
Yahoo!

879
01:05:24,962 --> 01:05:26,502
I'm driving!

880
01:05:34,513 --> 01:05:35,853
FRED:
Watch out, Scoob!

881
01:05:37,516 --> 01:05:39,226
SCOOBY:
Scooby-doo!

882
01:05:39,477 --> 01:05:40,767
[SCREECHES]

883
01:05:41,520 --> 01:05:43,360
VELMA:
You did it, Scoob!

884
01:05:49,236 --> 01:05:52,156
All right, gang.
The Monster Hive is right over there.

885
01:05:52,323 --> 01:05:54,453
Let's get this control panel
and plug her in.

886
01:05:54,617 --> 01:05:56,697
[HORSE NEIGHING]

887
01:06:10,341 --> 01:06:13,511
You go nowhere, knave.

888
01:06:14,762 --> 01:06:16,892
You guys take the long way around.

889
01:06:18,265 --> 01:06:19,675
And I'll hold him off.

890
01:06:22,269 --> 01:06:25,399
- Come on.
- Go get him, Fred.

891
01:06:29,902 --> 01:06:31,362
[BLACK KNIGHT LAUGHS]

892
01:07:34,967 --> 01:07:37,587
- Come on, Daph!
- I'm coming!

893
01:07:40,097 --> 01:07:42,467
Not so fast!

894
01:07:44,643 --> 01:07:48,983
You guys go. I'll take care of Sparky.
Just get that control panel to the Hive.

895
01:07:49,148 --> 01:07:51,358
- Go!
- We've got it, Daph!

896
01:08:03,370 --> 01:08:04,790
GHOST:
Ooh, scary.

897
01:08:04,955 --> 01:08:07,365
Taste the pain, Mr. Glowy Ugly Thing.

898
01:08:23,682 --> 01:08:25,182
Daph?

899
01:08:25,392 --> 01:08:28,352
- Daph, are you okay?
- I think so.

900
01:08:32,525 --> 01:08:34,395
Guess this is it, huh?

901
01:08:35,027 --> 01:08:36,357
Oh, baby.

902
01:08:38,405 --> 01:08:40,195
I'm afraid.

903
01:08:42,535 --> 01:08:44,195
What a wimp, huh?

904
01:08:45,162 --> 01:08:47,502
That doesn't make you a wimp.

905
01:08:48,916 --> 01:08:50,746
Makes you human.

906
01:08:54,797 --> 01:08:56,207
[SPEAKING INDISTINCTLY]

907
01:08:56,423 --> 01:08:57,723
VELMA:
The Skeleton Men.

908
01:08:57,883 --> 01:08:59,343
[SCOOBY FARTS]

909
01:08:59,677 --> 01:09:02,717
- He does that when he gets nerous.
- Sorry.

910
01:09:16,735 --> 01:09:20,025
- Here, Shaggy, take this.
- Why are you giving this to me?

911
01:09:20,197 --> 01:09:22,367
I'll distract those skeletal screwballs.

912
01:09:22,533 --> 01:09:24,873
- Get this to the Monster Hive.
- Us?

913
01:09:25,035 --> 01:09:27,075
VELMA:
Yes. You're faster than me.

914
01:09:27,246 --> 01:09:30,746
Once there, just plug it into the base.
Push this button.

915
01:09:30,958 --> 01:09:33,708
I fixed it so it will destroy
all the monsters.

916
01:09:33,878 --> 01:09:35,958
But... But...

917
01:09:36,463 --> 01:09:39,513
- we can't.
- We're screwups.

918
01:09:39,675 --> 01:09:42,335
We tried to be heroes like you guys,
but we're not.

919
01:09:42,511 --> 01:09:44,261
- We're just not.
- No.

920
01:09:44,471 --> 01:09:45,931
Like me?

921
01:09:49,101 --> 01:09:52,941
That's funny.
I always wanted to be like you guys.

922
01:09:54,106 --> 01:09:58,606
You guys are so free. You're never afraid
to be who you really are.

923
01:09:58,903 --> 01:10:03,783
Whether you're fearful or joyful or hungry.

924
01:10:05,242 --> 01:10:07,492
I think you've been heroes all along.

925
01:10:08,495 --> 01:10:10,245
You just haven't known it.

926
01:10:13,792 --> 01:10:14,792
Here I go.

927
01:10:19,423 --> 01:10:23,013
Heroes.

928
01:10:23,302 --> 01:10:25,642
On your knees, knave.

929
01:10:25,804 --> 01:10:27,474
Can't you see we're talking?

930
01:10:28,641 --> 01:10:31,021
Talking is for wimps.

931
01:10:33,312 --> 01:10:36,112
You can't fool me
with that macho façade.

932
01:10:36,649 --> 01:10:40,029
You're just afraid to show
your sensitive side.

933
01:10:40,486 --> 01:10:43,446
Ooh, you've touched my inner child.

934
01:10:44,657 --> 01:10:46,317
And he's really mad!

935
01:10:48,327 --> 01:10:50,657
- Come on, Scoob.
- Okay.

936
01:10:53,332 --> 01:10:57,672
- Miner 49er!
- Uh-oh.

937
01:10:57,920 --> 01:11:00,000
[LAUGHING]

938
01:11:04,301 --> 01:11:05,761
Eh?

939
01:11:12,559 --> 01:11:15,189
I'll get you, you varmints!

940
01:11:18,023 --> 01:11:19,483
Hey!

941
01:11:29,493 --> 01:11:30,953
Jinkies.

942
01:11:35,124 --> 01:11:37,214
[SPEAKING GIBBERISH]

943
01:11:42,881 --> 01:11:44,881
Dead end.

944
01:11:47,386 --> 01:11:50,596
Remember when we were young
and you used to wear that jumper?

945
01:11:52,224 --> 01:11:55,564
- What? Me? In a jumper?
- And we used to watch cable?

946
01:12:02,484 --> 01:12:03,744
FRED:
Do it!

947
01:12:09,116 --> 01:12:10,526
Lights out.

948
01:12:15,414 --> 01:12:16,914
Blackout! Blackout!

949
01:12:27,259 --> 01:12:28,259
Oh, crap.

950
01:12:37,686 --> 01:12:39,146
[SPEAKS INDISTINCTLY]

951
01:12:48,947 --> 01:12:51,947
Take this, daddy-o. It's a real gas.

952
01:12:52,201 --> 01:12:54,291
[SCOOBY FARTING]

953
01:13:02,961 --> 01:13:05,301
Come on. Let's go, Scoob!

954
01:13:06,090 --> 01:13:08,130
Ow-wee.

955
01:13:08,300 --> 01:13:10,130
My glasses.

956
01:13:10,636 --> 01:13:13,466
Oh, brother. Not again.

957
01:13:14,181 --> 01:13:16,811
I've got to consider contact lenses.

958
01:13:17,643 --> 01:13:18,683
What?

959
01:13:22,314 --> 01:13:24,404
[SPEAKING INDISTINCTLY]

960
01:13:36,328 --> 01:13:39,998
VELMA:
Some kind of scary bat.

961
01:13:41,834 --> 01:13:43,334
Wait a minute.

962
01:13:46,296 --> 01:13:47,836
That's the pterodactyl.

963
01:13:49,633 --> 01:13:51,633
The Pterodactyl Ghost.

964
01:13:55,013 --> 01:13:56,513
What's this?

965
01:14:14,992 --> 01:14:16,372
A shrine!

966
01:14:17,369 --> 01:14:19,869
To Jonathan Jacobo?

967
01:14:21,540 --> 01:14:24,250
But who would be so obsessed with him?

968
01:14:29,673 --> 01:14:31,383
PATRICK:
Velma.

969
01:14:32,217 --> 01:14:33,507
Lose something?

970
01:14:43,812 --> 01:14:45,062
Patrick.

971
01:14:48,192 --> 01:14:50,902
Uh, what are you doing here?

972
01:14:51,904 --> 01:14:54,574
I'm trying to solve this mystery.
Same as you.

973
01:14:56,074 --> 01:14:59,914
That is what you're doing, right?
Trying to solve this mystery?

974
01:15:00,078 --> 01:15:01,498
Yes.

975
01:15:03,290 --> 01:15:06,580
Why are you so obsessed
with Jonathan Jacobo?

976
01:15:08,712 --> 01:15:11,712
- What are you talking about?
- No way, Jose.

977
01:15:12,090 --> 01:15:13,300
Velma.

978
01:15:14,510 --> 01:15:16,590
Velma! Velma!

979
01:15:18,889 --> 01:15:20,559
Stay away from me.

980
01:15:21,934 --> 01:15:23,104
I know who you are.

981
01:15:31,109 --> 01:15:34,609
- Velma, let go of the grate.
- So I can fall to my death?

982
01:15:34,821 --> 01:15:36,451
No, so I can pull you up.

983
01:15:39,826 --> 01:15:43,446
- You gotta trust me.
- No. I only trust the facts.

984
01:15:43,622 --> 01:15:46,922
And all the facts say
that you're the Evil Masked Figure.

985
01:15:48,335 --> 01:15:50,285
What does your heart say?

986
01:15:50,462 --> 01:15:54,632
I don't know.
It's beating too loud for me to hear.

987
01:15:55,842 --> 01:15:58,472
Look deeper. You gotta trust me.

988
01:16:02,057 --> 01:16:03,467
[SCREAMS]

989
01:16:13,485 --> 01:16:14,775
You saved my life.

990
01:16:15,237 --> 01:16:17,317
[SCREECHING]

991
01:16:18,156 --> 01:16:19,446
Patrick!

992
01:16:19,658 --> 01:16:21,738
[SCREAMING]

993
01:16:22,869 --> 01:16:24,159
DAPHNE:
Velma!

994
01:16:24,371 --> 01:16:26,331
That thing just flew off with Patrick!

995
01:16:26,498 --> 01:16:30,668
The best we can do for him is get
that control panel back where it belongs.

996
01:16:32,462 --> 01:16:33,632
Where is it?

997
01:16:33,964 --> 01:16:35,514
I, uh...

998
01:16:35,674 --> 01:16:38,634
gave it to Shaggy and Scooby.

999
01:16:39,386 --> 01:16:43,806
That's weird. It sounded like you just said
you gave it to Shaggy and Scooby.

1000
01:16:54,860 --> 01:16:56,860
SHAGGY:
I think we lost them.

1001
01:16:58,530 --> 01:17:00,990
Scoob, we made it.

1002
01:17:02,200 --> 01:17:05,330
You should never have locked those locks.

1003
01:17:05,495 --> 01:17:08,035
Now you're stuck in here with me!

1004
01:17:08,206 --> 01:17:11,036
The Cotton Candy Glob.

1005
01:17:11,293 --> 01:17:14,503
- Cotton Candy Glob?
- Cotton Candy Glob?

1006
01:17:15,547 --> 01:17:17,207
Yes.

1007
01:17:24,014 --> 01:17:26,724
GLOB:
No! I'll give you cavities!

1008
01:17:26,892 --> 01:17:28,852
I don't see Shaggy and Scooby anywhere.

1009
01:17:29,019 --> 01:17:32,229
Poor guys are probably running around
helpless and terrified.

1010
01:17:34,149 --> 01:17:35,439
[SNEEZES]

1011
01:17:35,984 --> 01:17:37,824
This is like the greatest day...

1012
01:17:37,986 --> 01:17:39,566
- of our lives, Scoob.
- Yeah.

1013
01:17:39,738 --> 01:17:42,738
Finally, a monster
we could sink our teeth into.

1014
01:17:42,908 --> 01:17:47,748
I'm kind of thirsty. I wonder if there's
a Liter-sized Soda Glob anywhere?

1015
01:17:47,954 --> 01:17:51,254
- Come on, guys. We have to hurry.
- Come on.

1016
01:17:51,458 --> 01:17:54,208
We have to get this
control panel back before...

1017
01:17:56,088 --> 01:17:58,168
[GROWLING]

1018
01:18:01,510 --> 01:18:03,180
Before exactly that happens.

1019
01:18:03,345 --> 01:18:07,095
At last I have you, Mystery lnc.

1020
01:18:07,724 --> 01:18:11,854
You'll never make it past my monsters.

1021
01:18:12,020 --> 01:18:15,360
We've taken these jerks before, gang.
Let's do it again.

1022
01:18:17,359 --> 01:18:19,029
[SCREAMING]

1023
01:18:19,861 --> 01:18:24,121
DAPHNE: Fred!
- It's not them you need to worry about.

1024
01:18:26,493 --> 01:18:28,493
Now you are stuck in my trap.

1025
01:18:29,287 --> 01:18:30,867
FRED:
Daphne!

1026
01:18:33,792 --> 01:18:35,132
SHAGGY:
Daph!

1027
01:18:40,632 --> 01:18:42,092
Gotcha!

1028
01:18:43,802 --> 01:18:45,302
Go! Daphne!

1029
01:18:45,762 --> 01:18:49,522
Run, Velma.
Run, Velma!

1030
01:18:51,643 --> 01:18:53,523
Shaggy! Here!

1031
01:18:55,981 --> 01:18:57,021
Come on!

1032
01:19:00,527 --> 01:19:03,737
Soon your friends will be dead...

1033
01:19:03,905 --> 01:19:05,775
and Coolsville destroyed.

1034
01:19:06,533 --> 01:19:08,623
My revenge will be final...

1035
01:19:09,286 --> 01:19:12,656
and there's nothing you can do about it.

1036
01:19:13,165 --> 01:19:14,415
Help, Velma!

1037
01:19:17,502 --> 01:19:18,542
Daphne?

1038
01:19:20,797 --> 01:19:23,627
- Shaggy?
- Scoob...

1039
01:19:28,096 --> 01:19:29,756
[CACKLING]

1040
01:19:31,641 --> 01:19:33,101
Hmm.

1041
01:19:38,815 --> 01:19:40,565
Dude.

1042
01:19:42,861 --> 01:19:44,991
[GROANING]

1043
01:19:47,365 --> 01:19:51,195
- Like, frostbite never felt so good!
- Stop them!

1044
01:19:53,079 --> 01:19:55,829
- Go long, Scoob!
- Okay.

1045
01:19:58,877 --> 01:20:00,667
TAR MONSTER:
Here, doggy-doggy.

1046
01:20:02,672 --> 01:20:03,962
SCOOBY:
Rail glide!

1047
01:20:04,132 --> 01:20:07,222
TAR MONSTER: Watch this!
SCOOBY: Roll barrel!

1048
01:20:11,014 --> 01:20:13,104
[GROWLING]

1049
01:20:15,393 --> 01:20:16,733
Hang time!

1050
01:20:20,023 --> 01:20:22,903
End of the line, Doo!

1051
01:20:23,735 --> 01:20:26,235
Come here, you worthless mutt!

1052
01:20:32,744 --> 01:20:34,834
[GROANING]

1053
01:20:53,139 --> 01:20:54,219
SHAGGY:
Scoob!

1054
01:21:00,897 --> 01:21:02,187
You can do it, buddy!

1055
01:21:02,357 --> 01:21:03,767
[SCREECHING]

1056
01:21:15,537 --> 01:21:18,617
You can't do this to me!

1057
01:21:18,790 --> 01:21:21,460
Who do you think you are?

1058
01:21:22,294 --> 01:21:23,714
Scooby...

1059
01:21:23,879 --> 01:21:25,089
Dooby...

1060
01:21:25,255 --> 01:21:26,295
Doo!

1061
01:21:30,302 --> 01:21:31,972
No!

1062
01:21:57,329 --> 01:21:59,199
My monsters!

1063
01:22:06,504 --> 01:22:09,174
SHAGGY:
You did it! You saved us all!

1064
01:22:09,341 --> 01:22:10,631
I know.

1065
01:22:14,346 --> 01:22:16,466
[CHEERING]

1066
01:22:21,019 --> 01:22:24,359
Do you know the identity
of the Evil Masked Figure behind it all?

1067
01:22:24,522 --> 01:22:27,862
If our hunch is correct,
the Evil Masked Figure is...

1068
01:22:28,026 --> 01:22:29,226
No!

1069
01:22:33,865 --> 01:22:35,195
Heather Jasper-Howe.

1070
01:22:35,367 --> 01:22:37,197
Yeah. Huh?

1071
01:22:38,036 --> 01:22:40,996
But she was at the museum
when the Masked Figure was on the roof.

1072
01:22:41,164 --> 01:22:43,044
You almost had me there, didn't you?

1073
01:22:43,249 --> 01:22:46,789
Lucky for her, she had an assistant
helping her with her evil plans.

1074
01:22:48,546 --> 01:22:49,546
Ned.

1075
01:22:52,550 --> 01:22:55,140
When I realized
she was the Evil Masked Figure...

1076
01:22:55,303 --> 01:22:57,643
he quickly changed into her costume.

1077
01:22:57,806 --> 01:22:58,966
But why did she do it?

1078
01:22:59,140 --> 01:23:03,520
Because Heather Jasper-Howe
is actually...

1079
01:23:07,732 --> 01:23:10,232
Doctor Jonathan Jacobo.

1080
01:23:10,902 --> 01:23:13,322
The original Pterodactyl Ghost.

1081
01:23:13,488 --> 01:23:15,068
But how do you know this?

1082
01:23:15,281 --> 01:23:19,581
A photo, taken of Jacobo
in front of the Coolsonian.

1083
01:23:19,744 --> 01:23:23,084
Jacobo supposedly died
a year before construction even began.

1084
01:23:23,289 --> 01:23:26,789
So Jacobo survived that fall
off the prison wall.

1085
01:23:27,293 --> 01:23:29,923
He adapted the false
Heather Jasper-Howe persona...

1086
01:23:30,088 --> 01:23:31,668
to turn the press against us.

1087
01:23:31,840 --> 01:23:33,590
Then he framed Old Man Wickles...

1088
01:23:33,758 --> 01:23:37,218
by putting that book and
The Black Knight Ghost in his mansion.

1089
01:23:37,387 --> 01:23:40,597
As if you getting the lead
in My Fair Lady wasn't enough!

1090
01:23:40,765 --> 01:23:44,685
I was an excellent Eliza!
You were too act-y.

1091
01:23:44,853 --> 01:23:46,773
And stealing my Tater Tots!

1092
01:23:46,938 --> 01:23:49,018
You kept saying you felt puffy!

1093
01:23:50,066 --> 01:23:53,186
And the real identity of Ned is...

1094
01:23:53,945 --> 01:23:55,275
Ow.

1095
01:23:56,406 --> 01:23:57,696
Ned.

1096
01:23:57,907 --> 01:23:59,197
Huh?

1097
01:24:00,118 --> 01:24:04,248
I would have gotten away with it
if it weren't for those meddling punks...

1098
01:24:04,414 --> 01:24:05,964
and their dumb dog!

1099
01:24:06,124 --> 01:24:08,214
[CHEERING]

1100
01:24:11,129 --> 01:24:15,129
- You were a dude this whole time?
- Of course, dummkopf.

1101
01:24:15,967 --> 01:24:17,627
But we cuddled.

1102
01:24:23,475 --> 01:24:25,725
- Hi.
- Hi.

1103
01:24:26,978 --> 01:24:30,398
Listen, Velma, I know
that must have seemed very suspicious...

1104
01:24:30,565 --> 01:24:31,895
- but you've...
- No.

1105
01:24:32,067 --> 01:24:34,647
Got to believe me that
I had nothing to do with...

1106
01:24:34,861 --> 01:24:36,361
I trust you.

1107
01:24:37,155 --> 01:24:38,735
Listen, Patrick.

1108
01:24:39,991 --> 01:24:43,831
I'm not glamorous or mysterious.

1109
01:24:44,496 --> 01:24:46,246
But one thing that's true is...

1110
01:24:48,500 --> 01:24:50,250
that I like you.

1111
01:24:51,503 --> 01:24:52,843
Very much.

1112
01:24:54,589 --> 01:24:58,089
And I would like
to go out with you again.

1113
01:24:58,927 --> 01:25:02,177
But this time, I will go as myself.

1114
01:25:05,517 --> 01:25:08,807
Yeah, I'd like that, more than anything.

1115
01:25:10,188 --> 01:25:11,398
Okay.

1116
01:25:15,151 --> 01:25:18,611
[CROWD CHANTING]
Mystery Inc.! Mystery Inc.!

1117
01:25:19,030 --> 01:25:22,410
Hey. They're cheering for us again.

1118
01:25:22,617 --> 01:25:27,037
Yep. I always thought that was
the best thing in the world.

1119
01:25:27,205 --> 01:25:29,705
I guess I found something
a little bit better.

1120
01:25:31,376 --> 01:25:32,706
SCOOBY: Okay.
- Shaggy...

1121
01:25:32,877 --> 01:25:35,497
- can we get your photo in this?
- Yes.

1122
01:25:36,005 --> 01:25:38,045
[SCOOBY SPEAKING INDISTINCTLY]

1123
01:25:41,052 --> 01:25:43,142
[GROWLING]

1124
01:25:43,972 --> 01:25:46,312
Yikes! A monster!

1125
01:25:52,021 --> 01:25:55,571
- Like, Scoob, it's me, man!
- Shaggy!

1126
01:26:05,493 --> 01:26:08,083
Scooby-Dooby-Doo!

1127
01:26:10,415 --> 01:26:12,245
Sing it up, Ruben.

1128
01:26:12,458 --> 01:26:14,538
[SINGING "SHINING STAR"]

1129
01:26:16,671 --> 01:26:17,961
SCOOBY:
Everybody.

1130
01:26:39,944 --> 01:26:41,404
Come on, Shaggy.

1131
01:26:44,365 --> 01:26:45,865
Get down.

1132
01:32:23,788 --> 01:32:26,208
Game Boy Advance secret code.

1133
01:32:31,128 --> 01:32:32,628
[LAUGHS]

1134
01:32:44,809 --> 01:32:46,809
[ENGLISH - US - SDH]

